r.h2("2. Product Background")
r.p("Pickleball has become one of the fastest-growing recreational sports in Vietnam. Local press reported that the number of regular players nearly doubled during 2024 to about 30,000 [1], that more than 200 new courts opened in Hanoi alone in the first seven months of 2024 [2], and that Vietnam was listed among the ten fastest-growing pickleball nations by registered-player growth on the DUPR rating platform [3]. The sport attracts office workers, university students and older adults because the court is small and the basic strokes are easy to start with.")
r.p("The growth, however, is not matched by structured learning. Most newcomers learn by imitating other players on the court and receive no feedback on their technique. Qualified coaches are scarce and private lessons are expensive, so beginners often reinforce incorrect fundamentals – an overhand or late serve, dinks that float too high, volleys taken inside the non-volley zone (the \"kitchen\") – which are difficult to correct later. Casual players also find it hard to meet partners of a similar level, and they cannot practise when a court is unavailable because of weather, cost or schedule. Recent reports that some courts in central Hanoi are now under-used [4] suggest that players who do not progress tend to drop the sport.")
r.p("The project idea was proposed by the team members, who are themselves beginner and casual players, and was registered as a student-initiated capstone topic under the supervision of Mr. Lại Đức Hùng. The proposal identifies Vietnamese beginners and casual players as the users of the product; it names pickleball clubs, academies and community sport centres only as a possible later market, and the project does not target them (§4). PickleVerse addresses the problems above with a 3D game in which a player learns the rules and controls, repeats short graded drills, receives technique feedback computed from in-game telemetry, and applies the skills in matches against bots or other players.")

r.h2("3. Existing Systems")
r.p("The team studied three products that either simulate pickleball or help players improve their technique. They were selected because together they cover the three ideas that PickleVerse combines: an accessible pickleball game, a realistic training simulator, and AI-based technique analysis.")
r.h3("3.1 Pickleball Smash")
r.label("Link", "https://www.xbox.com/games/store/pickleball-smash/9N4DL8WL5DV2 [5]")
r.label("Overview", "An arcade pickleball game developed by 1PXL Games and published by GameMill Entertainment on 24 October 2023 for Nintendo Switch, PlayStation 4/5, Xbox One/Series X|S and PC (Steam) [5], [6].")
r.label("Actors", "Player (single player against the computer, or up to four players sharing one console).")
r.label("Main features", "Singles and doubles matches against computer opponents; local multiplayer; mini-games that each practise one shot; several playable characters and courts.")
r.label("Pros", "Simple controls and short sessions; mini-games show that a single activity can teach a single skill; available on many platforms.")
r.label("Cons", "Arcade physics rather than real pickleball technique; no lesson structure, scoring of technique or feedback; local multiplayer requires all players on the same console; no Vietnamese interface; no mobile version.")
r.h3("3.2 Eleven Pickleball")
r.label("Link", "https://www.meta.com/experiences/eleven-pickleball [7]")
r.label("Overview", "A virtual-reality pickleball simulator by For Fun Labs, the studio behind Eleven Table Tennis, released for Meta Quest headsets [7].")
r.label("Actors", "Player (single player against AI, or online against other players).")
r.label("Main features", "Physics-based paddle control with motion controllers; a programmable ball machine whose speed, spin and placement can be set for each shot; matches against AI bots; online 1v1 and 2v2 matches.")
r.label("Pros", "Realistic ball physics and paddle motion; the ball machine supports deliberate repetition of one shot; real online play.")
r.label("Cons", "Requires a VR headset, which few Vietnamese beginners own; no guided curriculum or star scoring; no technique diagnosis or recommendation; English interface.")
r.h3("3.3 PB Vision")
r.label("Link", "https://apps.apple.com/us/app/pb-vision/id6467020610 [8]")
r.label("Overview", "A mobile and web service that analyses videos of real pickleball games with computer vision and machine learning [8], [9].")
r.label("Actors", "Player (uploads a recorded game and reviews the analysis); club (records courts with an installed camera).")
r.label("Main features", "Shot speed, placement and error statistics; rally and shot breakdowns; heat maps and highlights; skill ratings.")
r.label("Pros", "Feedback is based on the player's real games; detailed statistics; integrates with club court cameras.")
r.label("Cons", "A full game must be filmed from a fixed angle with all four court corners visible; feedback arrives after the game, not during practice; no practice content when no court is available; advanced analysis is a paid service.")
r.h3("3.4 Comparison")
r.p("Table 3 compares the three products with PickleVerse against the criteria that matter to the target users.")
r.table(
    ["Criterion", "Pickleball Smash", "Eleven Pickleball", "PB Vision", "PickleVerse"],
    [
        ["Device needed", "Console or PC", "VR headset", "Phone and camera, real court", "Windows PC or Android phone"],
        ["Structured lessons with graded drills", "No (mini-games only)", "No (free ball machine)", "No", "Yes – tutorial and 15 lessons scored 0–3 stars"],
        ["Technique feedback", "No", "No", "Yes, after a filmed game", "Yes, after each drill and match, from in-game telemetry"],
        ["Practice without a court or partner", "Yes", "Yes", "No", "Yes, including offline training"],
        ["Online play and rating", "No online play", "Yes", "Rating only", "Yes – ranked singles and ranked doubles with Elo, custom singles and doubles rooms"],
        ["Vietnamese interface", "No", "No", "No", "Yes"],
        ["Operator tools (content, moderation, analytics)", "No", "No", "Club camera integration", "Yes – the project's administrators manage users, lessons, matches, reports and analytics"],
    ],
    widths=[3.6, 2.8, 2.8, 3.0, 4.0], size=9, first_col_bold=True, caption="Comparison of existing systems with PickleVerse")

r.h2("4. Business Opportunity")
r.p("The comparison shows a gap between entertainment games, which are accessible but do not teach technique, and analysis tools, which give useful feedback but require a real court, a recorded game and in many cases payment. A Vietnamese beginner who wants to learn the fundamentals at home, at low cost and in Vietnamese currently has no suitable product.")
r.p("PickleVerse targets this gap. It runs on hardware the users already own (a Windows PC or an Android phone), teaches the official rules through a tutorial and graded drills, and turns each drill and match into feedback without any camera. Because the feedback is computed from the game's own telemetry, the cost of a coaching session is close to zero, which makes the product attractive to price-sensitive students and young workers. Online ranked matches with an Elo rating and a leaderboard keep players engaged after the learning phase and help them find opponents of a similar level, which is a common complaint in local player communities. Following the Review 1 comments, a social feed lets players share posts with a replay of their own match or a training video, collect likes and comments, and message their friends, so that the game also helps players meet partners.")
r.p("PickleVerse is a consumer product: its customers are individual players, not organisations. The administration web application is used only by the project's own administrators, who also act as pickleball experts, to manage accounts, lessons, matches, player reports and analytics; it is not offered to clubs. The proposal mentioned clubs, academies and community sport centres as a possible business-to-business market because of their potential, but that direction is not part of the project: there is no club owner role and no club management in release 1.0 (LI-02), and the team has no plan to add one within the capstone. Cosmetic items are bought with an in-game currency.")
r.p("**Financing.** Review 1 asked how the product will be financed. The team answered with a paid membership (change request CR-01, §6.3), which has been in the product since 22/11/2026 as feature FE-11. It is a single payment of 49,000 VND with no renewal, made through the Vietnamese payment provider PayOS. It opens online play, private rooms and the adaptive bot for ever and adds 3,000 Elite Token to the wallet. Everything that serves the learning purpose of the product stays free: the tutorial, the 15 lessons, offline training, the coaching after drills and bot matches, bot matches at the three fixed levels, progress, the shop and the social features. The split keeps the promise to beginners (learn at no cost) and charges for the part that creates running costs, the dedicated game servers. The refund procedure, the terms of sale and the tax treatment are not settled yet (LI-14).")

r.h2("5. Software Product Vision")
r.p("**For** Vietnamese pickleball beginners and casual players **who** want to learn the rules and fundamental strokes without a coach, a partner or a court, **PickleVerse** is a 3D pickleball game for Windows and Android **that** teaches the rules through an interactive tutorial, trains each core technique with graded drills, gives technique feedback computed from gameplay telemetry, and lets players apply their skills in matches against adaptive bots and other players online. **Unlike** arcade pickleball games, which do not teach technique, and video-analysis services, which need a filmed game on a real court, **our product** combines practice, feedback and competition in one Vietnamese-language application that runs on devices the players already own.")

r.h2("6. Project Scope & Limitations")
r.h3("6.1 Major Features")
r.p("The eleven major features below define the scope of version 1.0; FE-11 was added on 22/11/2026 for change request CR-01. Report 3 refines each feature into use cases and functional requirements (FR-01 to FR-36), and the Review 2 commitment features F01–F18 are traced to them in Report 3, Appendix A.")
r.table(
    ["ID", "Feature", "Description"],
    [
        ["FE-01", "Account and onboarding", "Register with an email address, verify it with a six-digit one-time password (OTP), sign in and out, recover a forgotten password, edit the display name, choose a male or female character and choose a starting level (beginner or experienced) once. Configure audio, graphics, key bindings and the touch layout; on PC also choose windowed, fullscreen or borderless display. Quit the game from the login screen, the settings or the window frame. Since 21/11/2026 an account is used on one device at a time: signing in on another device ends the earlier session."],
        ["FE-02", "Tutorial and technique training", "A 17-step interactive tutorial on the court, the rules and the controls. Fifteen lessons in four groups (basic, control, advanced and doubles), each a group of one or more drills, train twelve techniques: serve, drive, dink, volley, power and cross-court modifiers, third-shot drop, reset, smash, footwork, approach, and doubles coverage and transition. Each drill is scored with 0–3 stars. Training also works offline after the first sign-in, and results are synchronised once when the game is online again."],
        ["FE-03", "Bot practice", "Singles matches against a computer opponent at three fixed levels (Easy, Medium, Hard) or in an adaptive mode whose behaviour-tree bot scales its shot choice, aggression and error rate to the player's Elo tier (membership required, FE-11). The player chooses a professional or outdoor court and day or night lighting. A referee call after each rally tells the player in red that the turn is lost, or in green that a point or the serve is won."],
        ["FE-04", "Online matches", "Needs the membership (FE-11). Ranked singles quick match that pairs players of similar Elo, with a match-found intro that shows both sides, a 10-second ready check and a bot opponent after 180 seconds without a human match; ranked doubles, a 2v2 search for a solo player or a party of two in which empty seats are filled with ranked bots after 180 seconds and Elo is computed against the average rating of the opposing team (clients of protocol 20 or later, since 17/11/2026); private singles and doubles rooms joined by room code or friend invitation, in which the next player becomes the host when the host leaves and two players can swap positions by agreement. Matches run on authoritative dedicated game servers – one container per match – and support reconnection."],
        ["FE-05", "AI coaching", "After a drill or match, the AI coaching service analyses the shot telemetry and returns a summary, detected errors (for example a late serve or a dink that is too high) and at most three recommended drills. The panel shows the number of shots, the clean shots and their rate, and every detected fault with its frequency and one piece of advice."],
        ["FE-06", "Progress, rewards and shop", "Experience points and levels, lesson stars, best accuracy and the four most recent accuracy results of each lesson, technique mastery, a daily play streak (rewarded through the achievement for a 5-day streak and a weekly streak mission), daily and weekly missions, achievements, and the Tokenpad currency. Players buy and equip cosmetic paddles in the shop and view owned items in the collection; two paddles, Gemstone and Dragon Ruby, have their own ball effect. The lobby plays ten copyright-free (NCS) tracks."],
        ["FE-07", "Social, history and ranking", "Send, accept and decline friend requests; remove and block players. A social feed with posts that contain text, a replay of one of the player's matches or an MP4 training video, shown to the community, to friends, to friends except selected players or to the author only, with likes and comments. Direct messages between friends with unread counters, and whispers to players who are in the lobby. Match history with the score of each game and the error statistics of each player, replays (recorded and uploaded while the match is played; pause, seek, 0.5×–2× speed) and the Elo leaderboard."],
        ["FE-08", "Reports, restrictions and appeals", "Report another player after a match. A restricted (suspended or banned) player can see the sanction decision and submit one appeal."],
        ["FE-09", "Administration web application", "Administrators manage accounts, roles and sanctions, reset player progress by group, manage lessons with their drills, technique references, cosmetics and missions, monitor and stop live matches, review player reports and appeals and open the replay of a reported match in the game, and view analytics (active users, retention, popular lessons, technique errors and matchmaking health)."],
        ["FE-10", "Expert review of AI results", "Administrators acting as pickleball experts label recorded shots and export a labelled dataset. This tool is used to evaluate the AI coaching quality (Report 3, NFR-06) and is an addition to the proposal."],
        ["FE-11", "Membership", "A player buys the lifetime membership (49,000 VND, one payment) from the menu or from a locked mode, pays on the PayOS page and returns to the game, which unlocks online play, private rooms and the adaptive bot and credits 3,000 Elite Token once PayOS has confirmed the full amount. Bought on Windows or in the directly installed Android app (change request CR-01; not in the Review 2 feature list F01–F18)."],
    ],
    widths=[1.4, 3.6, 11.0], size=9.5, first_col_bold=True, caption="Major features of PickleVerse 1.0")

r.h3("6.2 Limitations & Exclusions")
r.p("The following items are deliberately excluded from version 1.0, or deviate from the registered proposal. Each deviation is recorded with its reason so that requirement changes can be evaluated against it.")
r.table(
    ["ID", "Limitation or exclusion"],
    [
        ["LI-01", "Coaching uses in-game telemetry only. Analysis of real swing video, augmented reality and a separate coach portal are excluded."],
        ["LI-02", "Ranked seasons, tournaments, spectator mode and voice chat are excluded. Text communication is limited to direct messages between friends and whispers in the lobby (FE-07). Club owners and club management are not part of the product: the proposal named clubs only as a possible later market, and after Review 1 the team confirmed that it does not target them. Real-money payment is limited to the one-time membership of FE-11 (CR-01, implemented on 22/11/2026): currency packs, paid items, gifts and recurring subscriptions are excluded. The Tokenpad currency is earned only by playing. The Elite Token currency has one source, the 3,000 tokens credited when the membership is activated, so a player without membership cannot buy an item that is priced only in Elite Token."],
        ["LI-03", "Ranked Singles, Ranked Bot and, since 17/11/2026, ranked doubles change the Elo rating (K-factor 32, floor 100); in doubles the opponent rating is the average of the opposing team and only human players are rated. Practice bot matches and private rooms are unrated. The proposal described an Elo update after every match; rating only ranked results keeps the rating meaningful."],
        ["LI-04", "Offline mode covers training only, after at least one online sign-in on the device. Bot matches, online matches, the shop and the administration tools need a connection."],
        ["LI-05", "The proposal's \"self-assessment with a starting-tier classifier\" is implemented as a one-time choice between Beginner and Experienced. The trained tier model in the AI service is gated: its estimate is shown only when the model passes the accuracy target in NFR-06; otherwise the rule-based result is used."],
        ["LI-06", "Release platforms are Windows 10 or later and Android 8.0 (API 26) or later on ARM64. An iOS build is outside the delivered scope because the team has no Apple build machine and developer account; the project settings keep iOS 15.0 as the minimum for future work (the proposal named iOS 14)."],
        ["LI-07", "Each dedicated game-server container runs one match. The deployment starts as many containers as the setting PKV_GAME_REPLICAS (default 1) and the API reserves at most DedicatedServer:MaxConcurrentMatches matches (1 to 500); when every container is busy the players wait (\"server busy\"). The value used on staging has not been verified for this report. The proposal target of 500 concurrent matches would need 500 containers and has not been load-tested; it remains a scalability goal (Report 3, NFR-04)."],
        ["LI-08", "Technology deviations from the proposal: the web API uses ASP.NET Core (.NET 10) instead of Spring Boot or FastAPI because the team shares C# with Unity; real-time networking uses Photon Fusion 2 (shared lobby plus a dedicated server) instead of Netcode for GameObjects, after Netcode with Relay showed unstable connections during the October prototype; the game interface uses uGUI instead of UI Toolkit; ball flight uses a custom fixed-step simulation instead of PhysX for deterministic replay and server authority. The reasons are detailed in Report 4, §1.4."],
        ["LI-09", "The game interface is in Vietnamese only. The administration web application is in Vietnamese, and project documents are in English."],
        ["LI-10", "The proposal stated that stored data would be encrypted with AES-256. Version 1.0 protects secrets by one-way hashing instead (BCrypt for passwords, SHA-256 for refresh tokens, HMAC for verification and reset codes); the database files, backups and replay objects are not encrypted at rest. Disk encryption of the production host is planned before release (Report 4, §3.10)."],
        ["LI-11", "The proposal targeted 60 FPS on all devices. The SRS keeps 60 FPS for the reference PC but sets an average of 30 FPS for a mid-range Android phone (NFR-03), because mobile rendering removes HDR, MSAA and most shadows to stay within the phone's thermal budget; the game still requests up to 60 FPS on Android. Android APKs were built on 12/11/2026 and 14/11/2026, but on 17/11/2026 none has been installed, measured or smoke-tested on a physical device (test cases TC-N03 and TC-N10 are pending in Report 5). Both APKs use the online protocol 18, while the servers use protocol 22 since 21/11/2026, so a new APK is needed for online play; the higher detail of the courts and effects added on 24–25/11/2026 must be measured on the phone as well."],
        ["LI-12", "Uploading an MP4 training video to the social feed works in the Unity Editor and, since the fix of D-22 on 18/11/2026, in the Windows build through the Windows file dialog. The Android build has no video picker yet and shows \"Tải video hiện có trên bản Windows. Bản Android chưa hỗ trợ chọn tệp video.\" (video upload is available in the Windows build; the Android build cannot choose a video file yet). Text posts, shared replays and playing videos work on both platforms (Report 5, D-22)."],
        ["LI-13", "Review 1 suggested managing a schedule before online matches. The team decided not to adopt the suggestion: online play is real-time, so players meet through the ranked queue (with a ranked bot after 180 seconds), room codes and friend invitations, and a scheduled match would need presence, reminders and no-show rules that are outside the 14-week scope."],
        ["LI-14", "The membership (FE-11) covers the purchase only. Version 1.0 has no refund function, no list of orders in the admin web, no invoice and no terms-of-sale screen; a partial payment is not activated and is handled by hand. The server calls the production address of PayOS (api-merchant.payos.vn) and no test account is configured, so a payment on staging moves real money; test payments must be made by team members only. The purchase is offered on Windows and in the directly installed APK; a release on Google Play or the App Store would have to use the billing of the store."],
    ],
    widths=[1.4, 14.6], size=9.5, first_col_bold=True, caption="Limitations and exclusions")

